    {'id': 'eos.wilke_viscosity', 'name': "Gas mixture viscosity by Wilke's rule over Chung pure-component viscosities", 'kind': 'direct', 'assumptions': ['the per-component constants are those of the gas components intended, and the caller resolved them from the databank by name - this model takes the numbers, not the names.\n', "each pure-component viscosity is `eos.chung_viscosity`'s, evaluated at the *mixture* molar volume `V` - not at the component's own molar volume, which is what NeqSim's `calcViscosity` does.\n", '`z` is checked (non-negative, sums to one) rather than renormalised, so a composition error is a loud failure, not a silently different fluid.\n', 'the correlation is for a gas; the dense-gas term keeps it usable into the compressed region but not for a liquid.\n'], 'references': ['Wilke, C. R. (1950). "A viscosity equation for gas mixtures." Journal of Chemical Physics 18(4), 517-519. DOI 10.1063/1.1747673.', 'Chung, T.-H.; Ajlan, M.; Lee, L. L.; Starling, K. E. (1988). "Generalized multiparameter correlation for nonpolar and polar fluid transport properties." Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 27(4), 671-679. DOI 10.1021/ie00076a024.'], 'source': {'standard': 'Wilke, C. R. (1950); Chung et al. (1988)', 'edition': "Wilke's mixing rule is Wilke, J. Chem. Phys. 18(4), 517-519; the pure-component viscosity it mixes is Chung et al., Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 27(4), 671-679.", 'doi': '10.1063/1.1747673'}, 'inputs': {'Tc': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'K', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'critical temperature of each component\n'}, 'Vc': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'm**3/mol', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'critical volume of each component\n'}, 'M': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'kg/mol', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'molar mass of each component\n'}, 'omega': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'acentric factor of each component\n'}, 'dipole': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'dipole moment of each component, in debye\n'}, 'kappa': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'viscosity correction factor of each component\n'}, 'T': {'unit': 'K', 'description': 'absolute temperature\n'}, 'V': {'unit': 'm**3/mol', 'description': 'molar volume of the gas mixture at `T`\n'}, 'z': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'mole fractions; non-negative and summing to one.\n'}}, 'outputs': {'mu': {'unit': 'Pa*s', 'description': 'the gas mixture dynamic viscosity\n'}}, 'valid_range': [{'quantity': 'T', 'min': 0, 'min_inclusive': False, 'severity': 'error', 'rationale': 'an absolute temperature; zero and below are not states\n'}, {'quantity': 'V', 'min': 0, 'min_inclusive': False, 'severity': 'error', 'rationale': '`V` is the divisor in `y = Vc/(6*V)` inside the pure-component viscosity; a molar volume must be positive.\n'}], 'implementations': {'python': 'azoth.eos.wilke_viscosity', 'rust': 'azoth_eos::wilke_viscosity'}, '_path': 'specs/models/eos/wilke_viscosity.toml', 'cases': [{'id': 'methane_propane_equimolar_at_300_k', 'tolerance': 1e-09, 'source': "NeqSim 3.20.0 `ChungViscosityMethod.calcViscosity` for methane/propane 0.5/0.5 at 300 K, 10 bar, at the phase's molar volume.", 'inputs': {'Tc': [190.56, 369.83], 'Vc': [9.9e-05, 0.000203], 'M': [0.016043, 0.044097], 'omega': [0.0115, 0.1523], 'dipole': [0.0, 0.0], 'kappa': [0.0, 0.0], 'T': 300.0, 'V': 0.0022987856717900145, 'z': [0.5, 0.5]}, 'expected': {'mu': 9.543074369236108e-06}}, {'id': 'methane_butane_propane_at_350_k', 'tolerance': 1e-09, 'source': "NeqSim 3.20.0 `ChungViscosityMethod.calcViscosity` for methane/n-butane/propane 0.5/0.3/0.2 at 350 K, 15 bar, at the phase's molar volume.", 'inputs': {'Tc': [190.56, 425.12, 369.83], 'Vc': [9.9e-05, 0.000255, 0.000203], 'M': [0.016043, 0.058123, 0.044097], 'omega': [0.0115, 0.2002, 0.1523], 'dipole': [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], 'kappa': [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], 'T': 350.0, 'V': 0.0017565092156106297, 'z': [0.5, 0.3, 0.2]}, 'expected': {'mu': 1.0826970028242582e-05}}, {'id': 'methane_rich_propane_at_300_k', 'tolerance': 1e-09, 'source': "NeqSim 3.20.0 `ChungViscosityMethod.calcViscosity` for methane/propane 0.8/0.2 at 300 K, 10 bar, at the phase's molar volume.", 'inputs': {'Tc': [190.56, 369.83], 'Vc': [9.9e-05, 0.000203], 'M': [0.016043, 0.044097], 'omega': [0.0115, 0.1523], 'dipole': [0.0, 0.0], 'kappa': [0.0, 0.0], 'T': 300.0, 'V': 0.0023956252115606555, 'z': [0.8, 0.2]}, 'expected': {'mu': 1.0447753047985489e-05}}]},
    {'id': 'eos.wilson_activity_coefficients', 'name': 'Activity coefficients from the paraffin-wax Wilson model', 'kind': 'direct', 'assumptions': ['the caller supplies the molar mass and critical temperature - this model takes the numbers, not the names, the way `eos.wilke_viscosity` takes its constants.\n', "this is NeqSim's paraffin-wax (Coutinho) Wilson, not the classical fitted-`Aij` Wilson: the interaction energy is a correlation over carbon number and the sublimation enthalpy, so it needs no interaction-parameter table.\n", "`Lambda_ij = 1` when `i == j` or `M_i > M_j` - the branch in NeqSim's `getCharEnergyParamter` where the heavier first component collapses the exponent to zero - and `exp(-(lambda_j - lambda_i) / (R T))` otherwise.\n", "`T` must be below each component's `Tc`: the vaporization-enthalpy correlation is a power of `1 - T/Tc`, and a supercritical component yields NaN exactly as NeqSim does, which is not refused here.\n", '`x` is checked (non-negative, sums to one) rather than renormalised.\n'], 'references': ['Coutinho, J. A. P.; Andersen, S. I.; Stenby, E. H. (1995). "Evaluation of activity coefficient models in prediction of alkane solid-liquid equilibria." Fluid Phase Equilibria 103, 23-39.', "NeqSim - https://github.com/equinor/neqsim - Apache-2.0. `ComponentGEWilson.getWilsonActivityCoefficient`, the port source; NeqSim 3.20.0's `getActivityCoefficient` returns 0, so the oracle is the direct method.\n"], 'source': {'standard': 'Coutinho et al. (1995)', 'edition': 'Fluid Phase Equilibria 103, 23-39', 'doi': '10.1016/0378-3812(94)02603-Y'}, 'inputs': {'T': {'unit': 'K', 'description': 'absolute temperature\n'}, 'x': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'mole fractions; non-negative and summing to one.\n'}, 'M': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'kg/mol', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'molar mass of each component\n'}, 'Tc': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'K', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'critical temperature of each component\n'}}, 'outputs': {'ln_gamma': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'the natural logarithm of the activity coefficient of each component\n'}, 'gamma': {'type': 'vector', 'unit': 'dimensionless', 'length': 'one per component', 'description': 'the activity coefficient of each component\n'}}, 'valid_range': [{'quantity': 'T', 'min': 0, 'min_inclusive': False, 'severity': 'error', 'rationale': 'an absolute temperature; zero and below are not states\n'}], 'implementations': {'python': 'azoth.eos.wilson_activity_coefficients', 'rust': 'azoth_eos::wilson_activity_coefficients'}, '_path': 'specs/models/eos/wilson_activity_coefficients.toml', 'cases': [{'id': 'n_butane_nc12_equimolar_at_298_15_k', 'tolerance': 1e-09, 'source': 'NeqSim 3.20.0 `ComponentGEWilson.getWilsonActivityCoefficient` for n-butane/nc12 0.5/0.5 at 298.15 K.', 'inputs': {'T': 298.15, 'x': [0.5, 0.5], 'M': [0.058123, 0.1703], 'Tc': [425.12, 658.0]}, 'expected': {'ln_gamma': [0.19314718055973779, 0.49999935609153545], 'gamma': [1.213061319425015, 1.648720209074888]}}]},
